## Why No Changes Were Made

The project already has Vercel Web Analytics correctly configured according to the latest official documentation. The implementation follows best practices for vanilla HTML/JavaScript projects:

- Uses the `/_vercel/insights/script.js` endpoint (automatically served by Vercel)
- Script tags use `defer` attribute for optimal performance
- Properly commented for clarity
- Includes both Web Analytics and Speed Insights

## Next Steps for the Project Owner

To complete the analytics setup, ensure the following on Vercel dashboard:

1. **Enable Web Analytics**: Navigate to your Vercel dashboard → Analytics → select your project → click "Enable"
2. **Deploy**: After enabling, deploy the project to activate the analytics routes at `/_vercel/insights/*`
3. **Verify**: After deployment, check browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`
4. **Monitor**: Data will appear in your Vercel dashboard after several days of visitor traffic

## Technical Notes

- The frontend is deployed to GitHub Pages (static hosting)
- The backend is deployed to Vercel (serverless functions)
- Analytics scripts are loaded from Vercel's CDN when the frontend is accessed
- No code changes were necessary as the implementation is already complete and correct

## Conclusion

The Vercel Web Analytics integration is fully implemented and production-ready. No modifications were required as the existing implementation already follows the latest official Vercel documentation for vanilla HTML/JavaScript projects.
